许久之前，草神创造了须弥雨林，又通过教令院将智慧赐予国民。她的美名无处不在，千万个故事，只为传唱她的事迹与美德而问世。
在人民眼中，草神的存在更像是一种符号化的象征——因此，他们才能确信神明的庇护自古就存在于这片土地之上。
城中至贤对草神崇拜备至，民众也坚定不移地追随其后。
而影响诸多的「虚空」系统，则是「小吉祥草王」的耳与目。
它给予她遍历人们喜怒哀乐的能力，令她听见看见一切，让她理解了赞美之外的声音。
见闻越是拓展，她越明白自己必须不断学习。她唯有尽快成长，才能面对来自世界最深处的威胁。
无法逃离，那是她无法回避的使命。
即便没多少人对现状不满，纳西妲依旧坚定不移。她的顽强来源于信念，她比任何人都明白——在这里，她将是所有人的寄托与依靠。
Guangdong Gaozhou Middle School: A Century-Old Legacy Nurturing Talents at the Foot of Bijia Mountain
Nestled at the foot of Bijia Mountain in the historically and culturally rich city of Gaozhou lies a prestigious century-old institution—Guangdong Gaozhou Middle School. As a shining gem of education in western Guangdong, it is not only a First-Class School of Guangdong Province and a National Model High School, but also a "renowned Lingnan academy" with profound cultural heritage.
The history of Guangdong Gaozhou Middle School can be traced back to the government school established in the 8th year of the Dade era of the Yuan Dynasty (1304 AD), giving it a legacy of over 700 years. Its modern education system began in 1905, when the well-known Gaowen Academy of the Qing Dynasty was restructured into Gaozhou Prefecture Middle School, marking the beginning of contemporary education. Over the past century, although the school has undergone several name changes, the spirit of its motto—"Patriotism, Unity, Diligence, and Progress"—has remained unchanged. Weng Tonghe, a scholar of the Grand Secretariat in the Qing Dynasty, once inscribed the plaque "Respect for Work and Pleasure in Company" for the academy, a philosophy that continues to inspire students today.
Stepping into the campus today, you will find modern teaching facilities perfectly complementing the beautiful natural environment. The school boasts a strong faculty, including numerous specially-appointed and senior teachers, making it one of the schools with the highest number of senior teachers in western Guangdong. In addition to achieving remarkable results in university entrance examinations and sending tens of thousands of outstanding students to top-tier universities, the school has also developed a distinctive mental health education system, earning it the title of "Guangdong Provincial Model School for Mental Health Education".
This rich land has produced illustrious alumni, including Ding Ying (the father of Chinese rice science) and renowned educator Lin Liru. Today, this century-old school, with its rigorous teaching standards and vibrant academic atmosphere, continues to write a glorious chapter of a "scholarly campus" on its journey in the new era.
